From c03d44ce16e6330534ef9aee3873443717159611 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.slit (polecat)" <polecat-gastown.slit@soundit.local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:13:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add QBO expense and bank balance sync (psa-7v9)

QboSyncService previously synced only invoices. Add two pull-syncs from
QuickBooks Online, keeping the existing service/command/schedule patterns:

- syncBankBalances(): upserts Bank-type accounts (CurrentBalance snapshot)
  into qbo_bank_accounts, keyed by QBO account id.
- syncExpenses(?since): pages Purchase transactions into qbo_expenses,
  keyed by QBO purchase id. Optional Y-m-d lower bound (strictly parsed
  so it can't break out of the quoted QBO query clause).

Wiring:
- Models QboBankAccount / QboExpense + migrations for the two tables.
- Command `qbo:sync-financials` (--balances/--expenses/--since), mirroring
  qbo:sync-invoices; scheduled daily 05:40, gated on QBO being connected.
- Read-only "Bank & Expenses" page (controller + view + sidebar link) with
  an on-demand "Sync now" action.
- INSTALL.md scheduled-command entry.

Tests: bank-balance sync, expense sync (null-safe fields, idempotent upsert,
since sanitization), and the page/sync-action controller flow. 12 tests /
40 assertions, Pint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
